---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { SITE, SECTIONS, CONTACT } from '../data/site';
import { IMAGES } from '../data/images';
import { CITIES, COUNTRY_COUNT } from '../data/cities';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About Chandler | ${SITE.name}`}
  description="A Canadian from Atlantic Canada. In May 2022 I booked a one-month Airbnb in Tallinn, Estonia — and discovered that solo travel wasn't just something I wanted to do. It was something I needed to do."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-1">About</p>
      <h1 class="display-xl mb-2">Chandler</h1>
      <p class="body-lg measure">
        A Canadian from Atlantic Canada. In May 2022 I booked a one-month Airbnb in Tallinn, Estonia
        — and discovered that solo travel wasn't just something I wanted to do. It was something I
        needed to do.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ─── The story ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split split--wide-gap">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-2">The Story</p>
          <div class="stack">
            <p class="body-lg">
              It started in May 2022. I booked a month-long Airbnb on Narva Mantee in Tallinn,
              Estonia — a long, straight road running east from the old town. I had always known I
              wanted to travel, but that trip was when I realised it wasn't just a want. It was a
              need.
            </p>
            <p class="body-lg">
              I walked everywhere. I found the medieval old town, which is one of the best-preserved
              in Europe and somehow still feels lived-in. I took day trips to Tartu and Pärnu. I took
              the ferry to Helsinki and stood in the city feeling, for the first time, exactly what
              I was chasing with the way I dress. I went out, met strangers, ended up at an
              apartment party at 7am, and walked home at 8am as the city was waking up. I met people
              everywhere I went.
            </p>
            <p class="body-lg">
              That trip gave me something I hadn't fully had before: confidence. The knowledge that
              I could go somewhere completely alone and not just survive it but genuinely thrive. I
              fell in love with the European approach to life — laidback but functional, rooted in
              history, intentional in a way that's hard to find elsewhere.
            </p>
            <p class="body-lg">
              What followed was Iceland in September 2022, a four-month run across twenty-one cities
              in 2023, Iberia in 2024, and a return to Scandinavia in 2025 — {CITIES.length} cities
              across {COUNTRY_COUNT} countries so far.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:1rem">
          <img
            src={IMAGES.journey}
            alt="Chandler in a European cafe"
            style="width:100%; height:380px; object-fit:cover; object-position:center 30%"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <img
            src={IMAGES.travel}
            alt="A European street scene"
            style="width:100%; height:220px; object-fit:cover"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- ─── What the site is ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-1">What this site is</p>
      <h2 class="display-lg mb-2" style="max-width:600px">
        A catalogue, not a travel blog.
      </h2>
      <p class="body-lg measure-wide mb-4">
        This isn't a guide and it isn't researched. It's a record of what I've actually done and
        what I actually use — the cities I've walked, the cafés I kept going back to, the tours that
        were worth the day, and everything that fits in the bag. If I haven't been there or don't
        own it, it isn't here.
      </p>

      <div class="cell-grid cell-grid--tight">
        {
          SECTIONS.map((section) => (
            <a class="pillar-card card-hover" href={section.href}>
              <p class="pillar-card__num" style="font-size:3rem">
                {section.num}
              </p>
              <p class="pillar-label mb-1">{section.label}</p>
              <p class="body-sm">{section.description}</p>
              <span class="card-arrow">
                <Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} />
              </span>
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- ─── Transparency ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="measure-wide">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-1">Transparency</p>
        <h2 class="display-lg mb-2">How this works</h2>
        <div class="stack">
          <p class="body-lg">
            Some links on this site earn a commission — tour bookings, accommodation, and the
            occasional piece of gear. They're marked wherever they appear, they never change the
            price you pay, and they have no say in what gets listed. Nothing is on here that I
            haven't stayed in, gone on, or worn. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure" style="color:var(--c-accent)">affiliate disclosure</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="body-lg">
            Sections of this site are deliberately empty. Where there is no café, no tour, or no
            product listed, it's because I haven't written it down yet — not because there's nothing
            to fill the space with. Filling it with something approximate would defeat the point of
            the whole thing.
          </p>
          <p class="body-lg">
            CityboundNomad is an entity of Strandway Systems, based in Nova Scotia, Canada. If you
            want to get in touch, it's <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`} style="color:var(--c-accent)">{CONTACT.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="callout mt-3">
          “If I haven't been there or don't own it, it isn't on the list.”
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
